  "question": {
    "text": "In an atom, an electron is moving with a speed of $600 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$ with an accuracy of $0.005 \\%$. Certainity with which the position of the electron can be located is $\\left(h=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~m}^2 \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\\right.$, mass of electron, $e_m=9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{~kg}$ )",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "im9MO",
      "text": "\n$1.52 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wBLbj",
      "text": "\n$5.10 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{~m}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
